    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "By expanding $(1+2x)^4$ and substituting a value for $x$, show that\n$$\\binom40+2\\binom41+2^2\\binom42+2^3\\binom43+2^4\\binom44=3^4.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\binom40+2\\binom41+2^2\\binom42+2^3\\binom43+2^4\\binom44=3^4$.\n\nExpand $(1+2x)^4$ and substitute $x=1$.",
      "worked": "The binomial theorem gives\n$$\\binom40+2\\binom41x+2^2\\binom42x^2+2^3\\binom43x^3+2^4\\binom44x^4=(1+2x)^4.$$\nSubstituting $x=1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom40+2\\binom41+2^2\\binom42+2^3\\binom43+2^4\\binom44&=(1+2)^4\\\\\\binom40+2\\binom41+2^2\\binom42+2^3\\binom43+2^4\\binom44&=3^4.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
